cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this framework, please cite the associated article.
title: "Physics-Based Irradiance Transition Testing for MPPT Algorithms: simulation framework"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-28"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic simulation framework for evaluating maximum power point
  tracking (MPPT) algorithms under step, linear-ramp, and measurement-derived
  sigmoid irradiance transitions. It models a series string of three KC200GT
  photovoltaic modules with bypass diodes under four partial shading levels
  and evaluates Perturb and Observe, Incremental Conductance, and Spline-MPPT
  on tracking efficiency, steady-state error, power ripple, settling time,
  and GMPP acquisition time. It reproduces every result, figure, and table of
  the associated Solar Energy article.
